<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσημαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be seated at</i> or <i>close to</i>, c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώμασιν προσήμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1191
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νερτέρᾳ π. κώπῃ</span> ib.
				<i><span class="en">
				1617
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμοῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			: rarely c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρδίαν προσήμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					834
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>to be</i> or <i>lie near</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾶσοι . . τᾷδε γᾷ προσήμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					881
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>besiege</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύργοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					390
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
